@startuml
title MODRISS Operational Change Routing and Lifecycle Re-entry

skinparam backgroundColor #F5F3ED
skinparam shadowing false

start
:Capture roadmap request, telemetry signal, incident,\nsecurity finding, provider change or cost anomaly;
:Create WP-30 service work item on the Kanban board and preserve evidence;
:Classify maintenance purpose, emergency status and\nclass of service as independent axes;
:Replenish and pull under WP-31 WIP, capacity,\npriority and service-level-expectation policies;

if (Immediate restoration required?) then (yes)
  :Execute incident/recovery procedure;
  :Record temporary downstream change as open\nuntil removed or reconciled;
else (no)
endif

if (Disposition?) then (operations-only)
  :Resolve through operations procedure; verify evidence;\nclose WP-30 without creating a release;
elseif (bounded shortest safe MDE/release path) then (bounded)
  if (Outcome, requirement or domain meaning changed?) then (yes)
    :Re-enter at CIM;
  elseif (Provider-independent architecture changed?) then (yes)
    :Re-enter at PIM;
  elseif (AWS realization or deployment changed?) then (yes)
    :Re-enter at PSM;
  elseif (Reusable generation logic changed?) then (yes)
    :Re-enter at EGL/EGX generator source;
  elseif (Business logic or supported extension changed?) then (yes)
    :Re-enter at artifact/code workflow;
  elseif (Promotion, rollback or support control changed?) then (yes)
    :Re-enter at release/operations workflow;
  else (method concern)
    :Re-enter at method-engineering backlog;
  endif
  :Perform trace-based impact analysis and propagate\nthrough every affected downstream level;
  :Reconcile emergency change; obtain applicable G2–G7\nevidence; release and close WP-30;
else (planned release backlog)
  :Commit explicitly to a planned release backlog; retain\ntrace and acceptance intent in the release hypothesis;
endif
stop
@enduml
